  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A rigid diatomic ideal gas undergoes an adiabatic process at room temperature. The relation between temperature and volume for this process is $\\mathrm{TV}^{\\mathrm{x}}=$ constant, then $\\mathrm{x}$ is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "A6vkN",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{5}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Ub6p7",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{5}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7c2Qf",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "j4FuY",
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equation of adiabatic change is\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\mathrm{TV}^{\\gamma-1}=\\text { constant }\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nPut $\\gamma=\\frac{7}{5}$, we get: $\\gamma-1=\\frac{7}{5}-1$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{x}=\\frac{2}{5}$",
    "image": null
  },
